b'/F2 9.5 Tf' 40 419.0 Td (Q.1 \(b\) Solve the recurrence relation for Merge Sort using Master Theorem:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 405.5 Td (T\(n\) = 2T\(n/2\) + Theta\(n\). [10 Marks]) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 392.0 Td (Answer:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 378.5 Td (Master Theorem Form: T\(n\) = aT\(n/b\) + f\(n\)) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 365.0 Td (Here: a = 2, b = 2, f\(n\) = Theta\(n\) = Theta\(n^c\) where c = 1.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 351.5 Td (Calculate log_b\(a\) = log_2\(2\) = 1.) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 338.0 Td (Compare c and log_b\(a\):) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 324.5 Td (c = 1 and log_b\(a\) = 1 => c = log_b\(a\).) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 311.0 Td (By Case 2 of Master Theorem:) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 297.5 Td (T\(n\) = Theta\(n^\(log_b\(a\)\)  log\(n\)\) = Theta\(n  log\(n\)\).) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 284.0 Td (Hence, Merge Sort has a time complexity of O\(n log n\) in all cases \(Best, Worst, Aver) Tj
b'/F1 8.5 Tf' 40 270.5 Td (    age\).) Tj
